WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.160
Module five. E-way bills for high value orders, returns and disputes, and how the

2
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.285
Vendor gets paid.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.351
This module is about paperwork and money. It's less exciting than orders, but

4
00:00:14.351 --> 00:00:16.241
Mistakes here cost real money.

5
00:00:16.691 --> 00:00:18.761
First, when an e-way bill is needed.

6
00:00:19.211 --> 00:00:20.981
Then how the vendor uploads it.

7
00:00:21.431 --> 00:00:25.335
Then how the admin reviews, approves and emails it to the customer.

8
00:00:25.785 --> 00:00:28.836
Then returns and disputes, and what each status means.

9
00:00:29.286 --> 00:00:31.974
Then earnings, settlements and the Tally export.

10
00:00:32.424 --> 00:00:34.408
And finally, drivers and fleet.

11
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.932
Here's the rule. When goods worth fifty thousand rupees or more are transported, an

12
00:00:41.932 --> 00:00:47.064
E-way bill is required by law. So, when a vendor accepts an order of fifty thousand

13
00:00:47.064 --> 00:00:51.763
Rupees or more, that order automatically appears in the E-Way Bills section.

14
00:00:51.763 --> 00:00:56.957
The vendor generates the e-way bill on the government portal, uploads the P D F, and

15
00:00:56.957 --> 00:01:01.718
The admin reviews it. In Shiprocket, such orders also carry a tag: e-way bill

16
00:01:01.718 --> 00:01:02.336
Mandatory.

17
00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.845
Here's the full e-way bill flow, start to end.

18
00:02:03.295 --> 00:02:07.221
An order of fifty thousand rupees or more is accepted and packed.

19
00:02:07.671 --> 00:02:11.724
Its order I D appears in the E-Way Bills section as eligible.

20
00:02:12.174 --> 00:02:15.779
The vendor uploads the P D F and sets the valid till date.

21
00:02:16.229 --> 00:02:17.893
The status becomes submitted.

22
00:02:18.343 --> 00:02:22.525
The admin opens the P D F, checks it, and approves or rejects.

23
00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:27.412
Once approved, the admin can email the e-way bill to the customer directly.

24
00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.720
Let's watch this in the live demo.

25
00:02:34.733 --> 00:02:38.296
From Orders, the vendor opens E-Way Bills in the left menu.

26
00:02:38.896 --> 00:02:43.480
Each row shows the order, the e-way bill number, the valid till date, and the

27
00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:45.445
Status. These three are verified.

28
00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:56.781
Clicking upload e-way bill opens the attach to order window.

29
00:02:57.381 --> 00:03:03.300
The order I D drop down only lists eligible orders, fifty thousand rupees and above.

30
00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.682
Then the valid till date, and drag in the P D F.

31
00:03:07.282 --> 00:03:11.656
Here there's no eligible order yet, so the vendor goes back to Orders to check.

32
00:03:21.933 --> 00:03:24.280
Let's look at the e-way bills page once more.

33
00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:26.820
Upload e-way bill, the main button.

34
00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:30.044
Search by order I D or e-way bill number.

35
00:03:30.494 --> 00:03:31.859
The e-way bill number.

36
00:03:32.309 --> 00:03:37.840
Valid till. An e-way bill expires. If the delivery is delayed past this date, a new

37
00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:38.773
One is needed.

38
00:03:39.223 --> 00:03:42.316
And status: submitted, verified or rejected.

39
00:03:44.733 --> 00:03:46.653
Let's watch this in the live demo.

40
00:03:48.967 --> 00:03:53.901
Now a real one. The vendor attached the e-way bill for an order worth over sixty

41
00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:57.479
Four thousand rupees, and clicked submit for admin review.

42
00:03:58.079 --> 00:04:01.653
On the admin side, E-Way Bill Review shows the totals.

43
00:04:01.653 --> 00:04:03.903
One pending review, four approved.

44
00:04:04.503 --> 00:04:09.645
On the vendor side, the new row shows submitted, and a message confirms: e-way bill

45
00:04:09.645 --> 00:04:10.946
Submitted for review.

46
00:04:11.546 --> 00:04:17.172
Back in the admin panel. Each row has the e-way bill number, the vendor, the route,

47
00:04:17.172 --> 00:04:22.595
The value and the status. The actions are view the P D F, approve or reject, and

48
00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:23.002
Email.

49
00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:28.443
The admin views the P D F and checks the order, value and validity.

50
00:04:28.443 --> 00:04:29.358
Then approves.

51
00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:37.422
The vendor's list now shows verified.

52
00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:45.453
And the admin's counts update: zero pending, five approved.

53
00:04:45.453 --> 00:04:49.560
Now the admin can email the e-way bill straight to the customer.

54
00:04:52.867 --> 00:04:55.555
Here's the admin review page as a still picture.

55
00:04:56.005 --> 00:04:59.712
The counters: total, pending review, approved and rejected.

56
00:04:59.712 --> 00:05:01.722
Pending should not sit for long.

57
00:05:02.172 --> 00:05:03.687
The vendor who submitted it.

58
00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.225
The order value.

59
00:05:05.675 --> 00:05:06.614
The status.

60
00:05:07.064 --> 00:05:12.098
And the actions: view P D F, approve or reject, and email to the customer.

61
00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:18.895
When you review an e-way bill as admin, check these five things before approving.

62
00:05:19.345 --> 00:05:21.478
The order I D matches the order.

63
00:05:21.928 --> 00:05:24.467
The invoice value matches the order value.

64
00:05:24.917 --> 00:05:27.285
The vendor's G S T I N is correct.

65
00:05:27.735 --> 00:05:30.593
The valid till date covers the expected delivery.

66
00:05:31.043 --> 00:05:35.824
And the from and to pincodes are right. If anything is wrong, reject it, so the

67
00:05:35.824 --> 00:05:37.699
Vendor uploads a corrected one.

68
00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:44.132
Some tips for vendors, so their e-way bills get approved the first time.

69
00:05:44.582 --> 00:05:48.250
Generate the e-way bill on the government e-way bill portal.

70
00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.513
Oribrix does not generate it for you.

71
00:05:50.963 --> 00:05:56.280
Use the same invoice value as the order. A mismatch is the most common reason for

72
00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:56.936
Rejection.

73
00:05:57.386 --> 00:06:01.781
Set the valid till date so it covers the expected delivery, with a little buffer.

74
00:06:02.231 --> 00:06:05.303
Upload a clear P D F, not a blurry phone photo.

75
00:06:05.753 --> 00:06:10.387
And if it's rejected, fix it and upload again quickly, because the order can't move

76
00:06:10.387 --> 00:06:11.001
Without it.

77
00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:17.155
Now returns. A return request moves through these statuses.

78
00:06:17.605 --> 00:06:22.191
Pending approval. The customer asked for a return, and it's waiting for review.

79
00:06:22.641 --> 00:06:26.978
Picked up. This status comes from Shiprocket, when the courier collects the item

80
00:06:26.978 --> 00:06:27.953
From the customer.

81
00:06:28.403 --> 00:06:32.798
Refunded. This comes from Razorpay, after the admin approves the refund.

82
00:06:33.248 --> 00:06:38.111
Escalated. The admin marks it escalated when there's a problem, for example the

83
00:06:38.111 --> 00:06:41.867
Customer's return is wrong, or the vendor rejects the pickup.

84
00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:46.187
Let's watch this in the live demo.

85
00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:52.959
This is the vendor's returns page. Every return request is listed here.

86
00:06:53.559 --> 00:06:58.980
Each card shows the product, the return I D and order I D, the customer, quantity,

87
00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.559
Request date, refund amount and reason.

88
00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:09.531
View request details opens the full return, with its photos and status.

89
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:17.445
Scrolling down, statuses vary: pending approval, picked up, refunded.

90
00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:37.403
Reasons are recorded too, for example wrong item, or wrong quantity.

91
00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:49.168
And here's one marked escalated, which means the admin is handling it.

92
00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.984
Now money. Each settlement is one payout cycle.

93
00:08:00.984 --> 00:08:03.333
Opening one shows the full breakdown.

94
00:08:03.783 --> 00:08:06.237
The settlement period and the number of orders.

95
00:08:06.687 --> 00:08:09.332
Gross G M V, the total value sold.

96
00:08:09.782 --> 00:08:11.233
G S T collected.

97
00:08:11.683 --> 00:08:16.392
Return and refund deductions, and total deductions, such as logistics and

98
00:08:16.392 --> 00:08:17.101
Commission.

99
00:08:17.551 --> 00:08:21.016
The bank reference, called U T R, once the money is sent.

100
00:08:21.016 --> 00:08:24.421
The vendor can copy it to match with the bank statement.

101
00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:27.751
And net payout, what the vendor actually receives.

102
00:08:30.167 --> 00:08:32.087
Let's watch this in the live demo.

103
00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:38.752
Here's the earnings page in the live demo, and a quick look at Drivers and Fleet.

104
00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:42.479
Drivers and Fleet lists the vendor's own drivers.

105
00:08:42.479 --> 00:08:47.011
Total drivers, on trip, and idle. Each driver can be assigned an order.

106
00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:56.963
Back to Earnings and Settlements. On top: total settled payout, next payout,

107
00:08:56.963 --> 00:08:58.961
Deductions, and open disputes.

108
00:08:59.561 --> 00:09:06.140
Below, each settlement with its date range, orders, G M V, G S T, deductions, payout

109
00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:11.231
And status. Export Tally X M L and export C S V are on the right.

110
00:09:11.831 --> 00:09:15.948
Opening one settlement shows the full breakdown, with download statement.

111
00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:20.459
A settlement row can show one of these statuses.

112
00:09:20.909 --> 00:09:24.451
In progress. The current cycle. Orders are still being added.

113
00:09:24.901 --> 00:09:28.421
Settled. It has been paid, and the U T R is available.

114
00:09:28.871 --> 00:09:34.390
Tally synced. The data has been pushed to cloud Tally, so the accounts are up to

115
00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:38.599
Date. Exports for Tally X M L and C S V are always available.

116
00:09:40.983 --> 00:09:45.920
Quick check. A vendor accepted an order of sixty four thousand eight hundred ninety

117
00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:49.132
Six rupees. What extra step is needed? Think about it.

118
00:09:53.082 --> 00:09:57.783
The answer: upload an e-way bill for admin review, because the order is fifty

119
00:09:57.783 --> 00:09:59.248
Thousand rupees or more.

120
00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:03.863
Let's summarise module five.

121
00:10:04.313 --> 00:10:08.068
An order of fifty thousand rupees or more needs an e-way bill.

122
00:10:08.518 --> 00:10:13.309
The vendor uploads the P D F with a valid till date, and the admin approves and

123
00:10:13.309 --> 00:10:13.915
Emails it.

124
00:10:14.365 --> 00:10:18.269
Returns move through pending, picked up, refunded, or escalated.

125
00:10:18.719 --> 00:10:23.178
A settlement is G M V minus deductions, which gives the net payout.

126
00:10:23.628 --> 00:10:28.980
And everything can be exported for Tally. Next, in module six, account controls and

127
00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:29.367
Staff.

128
00:10:31.783 --> 00:10:37.288
That's the end of module 5. Next up, module 6: Account controls, staff and what's

129
00:10:37.288 --> 00:10:37.628
Next.
